<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rohida Fort</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Vichitragad</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rohida, also called Vichitragad, is a hill fort in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-ghats">Western Ghats</a> near Bhor in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pune">Pune</a> district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharashtra">Maharashtra</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shivaji">Shivaji</a> took it in the 1650s, and it later formed part of the territory of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pant-sachiv">Pant Sachivs</a> of Bhor, who held it until the end of princely rule.</p></div>
